# THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH FOR BACKEND CONFIGURATION.
#
# The deploy workflow reads the keys below, resolves each one from GitHub
# Variables or Secrets, and FAILS THE BUILD if a required value is missing or
# empty. Adding a variable here and wiring it in GitHub is therefore enough --
# there is no second list to keep in step.
#
# This replaces the old arrangement, where the workflows wrote backend/.env
# from a fixed heredoc and scp'd it over on every run. A variable added in
# GitHub did nothing until someone remembered to edit the heredoc too, and the
# app then read an empty string and behaved as though the feature had never
# been configured -- no error, just wrong behaviour. See docs/deployment.md.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line. A line ending in "# optional" may be empty
# in a deployed environment; everything else must have a value.

# --- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development points at the compose Postgres service by name. In a
# deployed environment this is the shared Postgres CONTAINER over the Docker
# network -- not localhost, which is what it meant while the database ran on
# bare metal.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://ticketing_dev:ticketing_dev@postgres:5432/ticketing_saas

# --- Clerk ----------------------------------------------------------------
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
CLERK_FRONTEND_API=https://your-app-name.clerk.accounts.dev

# --- Application ----------------------------------------------------------
# development | test | prod. Gates FastAPI's /docs (off in prod only) and
# which accounts get the custom board.
ENVIRONMENT=development

# The two accounts the app knows individually -- there is no admin ROLE.
# Compared case-folded, because they are hand-typed into deploy config. Empty
# means "nobody", which is the correct default: an unset value must mean the
# feature is off, never a guess.
ADMIN_EMAIL=  # optional
MANAGER_EMAIL=  # optional
